\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1.\cf0   Am I pleased with the fact
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 That I'm born human?
\par For the sake of my life
\par Should I be pleased?
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Yes, it pleases me that
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 I am born human?
\par But the journey I make
\par Become always hard.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. These our earthly problems,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 Great troubles and pains;
\par For we live in sadness
\par Till the time we die.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Its befitting for us
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 To really weep;
\par But Jesus has come,
\par In order to save us.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. The crucified Jesus
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 Was hanged for sinners;
\par You love me the wretched,
\par Give me your freedom.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. You have called me also
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 To sit beside you.
\par No other person can
\par Take me from your hands
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 7\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 7.  My uncountable sins,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 you forgave me all.
\par You have been directing me
\par The path to heav'n.
\par \pard\li360\sl190\slmult0 
\par \pard\fi-270\li360\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 8\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  8. Now, I have seen Jesus
\par \pard\li360\sl190\slmult0 As my Good Saviour.
\par He alone can save me
\par I'll look to Jesus
\par 
\par \pard\fi-315\li360\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 9\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 9. Yes, it pleases me that
\par \pard\li360\sl190\slmult0 I am born human.
\par You also my neighbours,
\par Depend on Jesus.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-270\li360\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 10\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 10.  The Christian lives in peace,
\par \pard\li360\sl190\slmult0 Despite bitter times;
\par He looks to the heavens
\par In his tribulations.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-270\li360\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 11\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 11. The Lord Jesus keeps watch
\par \pard\li360\sl190\slmult0 Over him from heaven;
\par And He strengthens him,
\par To tread upon his path
\par 
\par \pard\fi-270\li360\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 12\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 12. To your destination,
\par \pard\li360\sl190\slmult0 He will hold your hand,
\par And take you to heaven.
\par So to live with Him.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-270\li360\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 13\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 13. Tribulations have passed,
\par \pard\li360\sl190\slmult0 You'll always rejoice
\par We shall look to Jesus
\par \pard      And praise him always.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs14 
\par }

